I’ve identified why the isolated entry run is not terminating: selecting only `SPEC.derivative-entry` removes the `derivative-loop` reachability claim that serves as its circularity, so this diagnostic is unrolling the unbounded loop instead of testing the submitted proof set. I’m stopping that non-target diagnostic and will run the complete positive spec; the loop claim already closes alone, while the entry claim must be checked with its declared helper claim present.
